venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Generated/downloaded artifacts. Two subsets are committed despite that,
# for deploy reliability (Streamlit Community Cloud clones a fresh repo
# with no local generation step, and synth/*.py's text rendering hardcodes
# C:\Windows\Fonts paths -- unusable on that Linux container even if we
# tried to regenerate on boot): the demo corpus (data/documents, data/forged)
# and the model/glyph files below. Everything else stays ignored --
# data/pki/ specifically holds real, unencrypted demo signing keys and must
# never be committed; data/portraits/ holds real consenting-person face
# photos; results/ is session-local ledger output.
data/*
!data/documents/
!data/documents/**
!data/forged/
!data/forged/**
# data/registry/registry.db is synthetic data, committed like documents/
# above. data/registry/manifest.json is NOT: it's an ECDSA signature tied
# to whichever demo PKI key generated it (data/pki/, gitignored, one
# random keypair per machine) -- see core/issuer/integrity.py's docstring
# for why a manifest signed on one machine would fail verification on
# another. It's regenerated lazily, per machine, same as data/pki/ itself.
!data/registry/
data/registry/*
!data/registry/registry.db
models/*
!models/*.onnx
!models/*.npz
results/

*.log
.DS_Store

# working plan files -- not part of the shipped project
PLAN_*.md
